                  poorly calibrated algorithms can be misleading and potentially
                  harmful for clinical decision-making. We summarize how to
                  avoid poor calibration at algorithm development and how to
                  assess calibration at algorithm validation, emphasizing
                  balance between model complexity and the available sample
                  size. At external validation, calibration curves require
