  issn         = {1878-5921,0895-4356},
  abstract     = {OBJECTIVES: When developing a clinical prediction model,
                  penalization techniques are recommended to address
                  overfitting, as they shrink predictor effect estimates toward
                  the null and reduce mean-square prediction error in new
                  individuals. However, shrinkage and penalty terms ('tuning
                  parameters') are estimated with uncertainty from the
